<WovenDocs::Page
  @id="field"
  @title="Field and form layout"
  @subtitle="Label, hint, error and help around any control; action rows and filter rows."
  @components="Woven::Field, Woven::FieldGroup, Woven::FormActions"
>
  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Overview" @id="overview">
    <p class="woven-doc__intro">
      Field wires a label to whatever control it wraps. A native input,
      textarea or select gets a
      <code class="wu-code">for</code>/<code class="wu-code">id</code>
      pair; a combobox, listbox or button gets
      <code class="wu-code">aria-labelledby</code>. The optional help
      button renders outside the label element on purpose, because anything
      inside a label joins the control's accessible name. Every form control
      on a page belongs inside a Field.
    </p>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Features" @id="features">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Label, required marker, hint and error; the error replaces the hint on a line the kit live field always reserves.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Validation status (error, warning, success) wired to aria-invalid and aria-describedby on any control.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Floating label mode, and FieldGroup for radio and checkbox sets.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Automatic label association for native and ARIA controls.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Horizontal layout.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Label help button that opens a native popover.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>FormActions aligns a button row; wu-field-row and wu-filter-row lay out rows of fields.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Field: label and text" @id="field-text">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Label"
      @note="The minimum: a label linked to the control by for and id. The default for every form field."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.label}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @label="Property name">
        <Woven::Input @placeholder="Marina Tower" />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Required"
      @note="Sets aria-required on the control, so assistive technology announces it, and the kit draws the label asterisk from that attribute. Add the native required attribute too when the browser should block submit."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.required}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @label="Property name" @required={{true}}>
        <Woven::Input @placeholder="Marina Tower" />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Hint"
      @note="Helper text under the control for format or consequence, shown while there is no error."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.hint}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @label="Property name" @hint="Shown to tenants on the portal">
        <Woven::Input @placeholder="Marina Tower" />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Error"
      @note="Replaces the hint with the validation message and the kit error marker. The control gets aria-invalid and the danger border automatically."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.error}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @label="Monthly rent" @hint="Whole dirhams" @error="Rent must be greater than 0">
        <Woven::Input @value="-100" />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Validation" @id="validation">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Status"
      @note="The status argument takes error, warning or success. Field writes aria-invalid, aria-describedby and data-wu-field-status onto the control; only error is styled, through aria-invalid, so the border always matches what assistive technology hears. A warning hint renders as info. A non-empty error message implies error."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.statuses}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @label="Monthly rent" @hint="Whole dirhams">
        <Woven::Input @value="85000" data-test-woven-status-none />
      </Woven::Field>
      <Woven::Field @label="Monthly rent" @error="Enter a rent greater than 0">
        <Woven::Input @value="-100" data-test-woven-status-error />
      </Woven::Field>
      <Woven::Field @label="Monthly rent" @status="warning" @hint="Above the area average; check the amount">
        <Woven::Input @value="400000" data-test-woven-status-warning />
      </Woven::Field>
      <Woven::Field @label="Monthly rent" @status="success" @hint="Matches the signed lease">
        <Woven::Input @value="85000" data-test-woven-status-success />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Every control"
      @note="Select, Dropdown, Checkbox and Toggle take the same status from the Field around them."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.statusControls}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @label="Region" @error="Choose a region">
        <Woven::Select @options={{this.regionOptions}} @placeholder="Choose a region" data-test-woven-status-select />
      </Woven::Field>
      <Woven::Field @label="Status" @error="Choose a status">
        <Woven::Dropdown @align="start" @options={{this.filterStatusOptions}} @placeholder="All" data-test-woven-status-dropdown />
      </Woven::Field>
      <Woven::Field @label="Terms" @error="Accept the terms to continue">
        <Woven::Checkbox @label="I accept the terms" data-test-woven-status-checkbox />
      </Woven::Field>
      <Woven::Field @label="Notify tenants" @status="warning" @hint="Tenants will not hear about rent changes">
        <Woven::Toggle @checked={{false}} data-test-woven-status-toggle />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Live message line and numeric keyboard"
      @note="Every Field renders the kit live modifier, which always reserves one message line, so a hint or error appears without moving anything below it. Type a letter to see the error. @inputmode=&quot;numeric&quot; opens the number pad for a code that is not a quantity."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.liveError}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @label="Cheque number" @hint="Six digits" @error={{this.chequeError}} @required={{true}}>
        <Woven::Input
          @value={{this.chequeNumber}}
          @inputmode="numeric"
          @onInput={{this.setChequeNumber}}
          pattern="[0-9]*"
          data-test-woven-cheque
        />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Floating label" @id="floating-label">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Placeholder as label"
      @note="Without @label, @placeholder becomes a real label inside the control. It rises onto the top border on focus or once there is a value, and never disappears. Format guidance belongs in @hint. Pass the yielded placeholder to a Select or Autocomplete."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.floating}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @placeholder="Property name" @hint="Shown to tenants on the portal">
        <Woven::Input data-test-woven-floating-input />
      </Woven::Field>
      <Woven::Field @placeholder="Region" as |f|>
        <Woven::Select @options={{this.regionOptions}} @placeholder={{f.placeholder}} data-test-woven-floating-select />
      </Woven::Field>
      <Woven::Field @placeholder="Notes">
        <Woven::Textarea data-test-woven-floating-textarea />
      </Woven::Field>
      <Woven::Field @placeholder="Building" @error="Choose a building" as |f|>
        <Woven::Autocomplete @options={{this.buildings}} @placeholder={{f.placeholder}} data-test-woven-floating-autocomplete />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Field group" @id="field-group">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Radios with an error"
      @note="FieldGroup renders a fieldset and legend with one message. @required marks the radios required, and the kit draws the legend asterisk. Its status reaches every control inside; the message ids go on the fieldset."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.fieldGroup}}
    >
      <Woven::FieldGroup
        @label="Payment method"
        @required={{true}}
        @error={{if this.paymentMethod null "Choose how the tenant pays"}}
        data-test-woven-field-group
      >
        <div class="wu-check-group">
          <Woven::Radio
            @name="woven-pay"
            @value="cheque"
            @label="Cheque"
            @checked={{eq this.paymentMethod "cheque"}}
            @onChange={{this.setPaymentMethod}}
          />
          <Woven::Radio
            @name="woven-pay"
            @value="transfer"
            @label="Bank transfer"
            @checked={{eq this.paymentMethod "transfer"}}
            @onChange={{this.setPaymentMethod}}
          />
        </div>
      </Woven::FieldGroup>
    </WovenDocs::Example>
    <h3 class="woven-subtitle">FieldGroup arguments</h3>
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="args" @rows={{this.groupArgRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Autofill and keyboards" @id="autofill">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Browser autofill keeps the surface color and regular text color in both themes; the focus ring and status borders stay visible over it.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Phones: type="tel" with @inputmode="tel". Codes, OTPs, cheque and postal numbers: type="text" with @inputmode="numeric" and pattern="[0-9]*". Money and quantities keep type="number".</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Field: layout" @id="field-layout">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Horizontal"
      @note="Label beside the control, for settings panels and short forms where vertical space matters."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.horizontal}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @label="Region" @horizontal={{true}}>
        <Woven::Select @options={{this.regionOptions}} @placeholder="Choose a region" />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Field: help" @id="field-tooltip">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Label help"
      @note="The kit wu-field-help button beside the label opens the text in a native popover, by click, touch or keyboard. For definitions too long for a hint; the button stays outside the label so it does not become part of the control's name."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.tooltip}}
    >
      <Woven::Field
        @label="Tenancy Registration Ref"
        @tooltip="e.g. Ejari in Dubai, Tawtheeq in Abu Dhabi, or your local government lease registry number."
      >
        <Woven::Input @placeholder="TR-2026-00001" />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Field: non-native controls" @id="field-aria">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Combobox"
      @note="A Dropdown has no native input to label, so the field sets aria-labelledby on the combobox or trigger button, skipping the help button."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.combobox}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @label="Status">
        <Woven::Dropdown @align="start" @options={{this.filterStatusOptions}} @placeholder="All" />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Toggle"
      @note="A toggle's native input receives the label id, so the field label names it and the horizontal layout reads as a settings row."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.toggle}}
    >
      <Woven::Field @label="Notify tenants" @horizontal={{true}}>
        <Woven::Toggle @checked={{this.notify}} @onChange={{this.setNotify}} />
      </Woven::Field>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <h3 class="woven-subtitle">Field arguments</h3>
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="args" @rows={{this.fieldArgRows}} />
    <h3 class="woven-subtitle">Field blocks</h3>
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="blocks" @rows={{this.fieldBlockRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Filter row" @id="filter-row">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Responsive filter bar"
      @note="An auto-fitting grid whose column count follows the viewport. The unlabeled control takes a wu-field-label visually-hidden label to share the baseline. Use it above every list."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.filterRow}}
    >
      <div class="wu-filter-row">
        <Woven::Field @label="Status">
          <Woven::Dropdown
            @align="start"
            @value={{this.filterStatus}}
            @onSelect={{this.setFilterStatus}}
            @options={{this.filterStatusOptions}}
            @placeholder="All"
          />
        </Woven::Field>
        <Woven::Field @label="Search">
          <Woven::Input
            @value={{this.filterSearch}}
            @onInput={{this.setFilterSearch}}
            @placeholder="Name or ID"
          />
        </Woven::Field>
        <div class="wu-field">
          <label class="wu-field-label visually-hidden">Actions</label>
          <Woven::Button
            @text="Clear"
            @onClick={{this.clearFilters}}
            data-test-woven-clear-filters
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </WovenDocs::Example>
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="classes" @rows={{this.classRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Form actions" @id="form-actions">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Start aligned"
      @note="The default: buttons at the inline start, primary first. For forms that read top to bottom on the page."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.actionsStart}}
    >
      <Woven::FormActions>
        <Woven::Button @variant="brand" @text="Save" />
        <Woven::Button @text="Cancel" />
      </Woven::FormActions>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="End aligned"
      @note="Buttons at the inline end with the primary last, the dialog and drawer convention."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.actionsEnd}}
    >
      <Woven::FormActions @align="end">
        <Woven::Button @text="Cancel" />
        <Woven::Button @variant="brand" @text="Save" />
      </Woven::FormActions>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Between"
      @note="A destructive action at one edge and the primary at the other, so they cannot be hit by mistake."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.actionsBetween}}
    >
      <Woven::FormActions @align="between">
        <Woven::Button @variant="ghost" @text="Delete" />
        <Woven::Button @variant="brand" @text="Save changes" />
      </Woven::FormActions>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <h3 class="woven-subtitle">Form actions arguments</h3>
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="args" @rows={{this.actionsArgRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Accessibility" @id="accessibility">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The label receives a stable id and a for attribute pointing at the control; an existing id on the control is respected.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The required asterisk is drawn in CSS from aria-required, which the field sets on the control, so assistive technology announces it.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The help button is labeled "More information about {label}", opens its popover by click, touch or keyboard, and is skipped when the dialog focus trap picks a first control.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The control receives aria-invalid while the status is error, aria-describedby pointing at the hint or error (caller ids are kept after them), and aria-required with @required.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The active message id joins aria-describedby, so it is read when the control is focused; the error icon is aria-hidden and color is never the only signal.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="RTL" @id="rtl">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Horizontal fields place the label on the inline-start side, so it moves to the right under dir="rtl".</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The filter row grid and FormActions alignment are logical: end alignment sits on the left in RTL.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The floating label is placed with logical insets and moves only vertically, so it needs no mirroring.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>
</WovenDocs::Page>
